## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 3 |
| **Medium** | 2 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This suite is a **textbook coverage-touching test class**. All 10 public methods of `ProductCatalog` are called, producing ~95% line coverage, but **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions** and the remaining 4 assert only `IsNotNull` — a condition that can virtually never fail given the production code. These tests cannot catch regressions.

---

### Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)

**Location:** Entire class (lines 17–89)

Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called in declaration order with no meaningful verification. This is the exact pattern inflating your coverage metric while bugs escape to production.

| Test | Assertions | Verdict |
|------|------------|---------|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | **0** | Proves nothing |
| `GetProduct_Works` (L23) | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks Sku/Name/Price |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L31) | **0** | Never verifies price changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38) | **0** | Never verifies product is gone |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (L45) | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks result count or content |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (L54) | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks count |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L62) | **0** | Doesn't even capture the return value meaningfully |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68) | **0** | Never verifies prices were discounted |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (L76) | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks CSV content |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L84) | **0** | Never verifies products were imported |

#### 2. No Assertions (6 tests)

**Locations:** Lines 17, 31, 38, 62, 68, 84

These tests pass regardless of what the production code does. Example fix for `UpdatePrice_Works`:

```csharp
// BEFORE (line 31-36)
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_Works()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
}

// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_UpdatesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
}
```

Example fix for `RemoveProduct_Works`:

```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_ProductNoLongerRetrievable()
{
